# Suite machine (plans 03-02..03-12): machine-level cases in one executable (D-15). Family
# sha256 (plan 03-02): core SHA-256 against independent literal digests, one case per line of
# data/sha256/vectors.txt plus the invariance, context and reset cases (D-28, A-04).
# Family create (plan 03-09): storage requirements, create, info and destroy through the public
# header, their refusals (whole-storage comparison), status names and the API version.
# Family digest (plan 03-09): the canonical state digest (D-35): literal streams, composite
# framing, field-table coverage, per-domain sensitivity, padding and the digest refusals.
# Family load (plan 03-10): typed EXEC, GROM and IVSC cartridge loads through the public header
# with generated stand-in bytes (D-24), their reports and digests, layer 2, the load options and
# unload back to the fresh state.
